      "description": "Watch Hoffenheim vs Borussia Dortmund highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 5, 2026. The atmosphere at the PreZero Arena was electric for this Bundesliga clash on September 5, 2026 , as Hoffenheim and Borussia Dortmund squared off in a match defined by tactical shifts and relentless energy. With 30,150 fans in attendance, the game delivered a narrative filled with unexpected twists that kept everyone guessing until the final whistle. Tactical Battle and the Breakthrough The first half saw Hoffenheim controlling much of the ball, maintaining 60% possession while searching for a gap in the Borussia Dortmund structure. Early chances were exchanged, with Maximilian Beier seeing a header comfortably saved by Oliver Baumann , while at the other end, Adam Hlozek tested Gregor Kobel . The deadlock was finally broken in the 45th minute in spectacular fashion. Leon Avdullahu found space outside the box and unleashed a right-footed strike following a setup by Vladimir Coufal , sending the home side into the tunnel with a hard-earned lead. Second Half Surge and the Dortmund Response The momentum stayed with the hosts early in the second period. In the 54th minute, Tim Lemperle doubled the advantage for Hoffenheim with a deflected shot, assisted by Adam Daghim . Facing a two-goal deficit, Borussia Dortmund refused to fold. The comeback trail began in the 61st minute when Serhou Guirassy capitalized on a defensive lapse by Leon Avdullahu to clinical finish. The momentum shifted instantly, and just five minutes later, substitute Fabio Silva leveled the score with a clinical left-footed finish, with Guirassy turning provider this time. Late Drama and a Cruel Twist As the match entered its final stages, the intensity boiled over, resulting in a flurry of yellow cards for players including Wouter Burger , Maximilian Beier , and Andrej Kramaric . The defining moment arrived in the 86th minute, but not through a piece of brilliance. Albian Hajdari inadvertently directed the ball into his own net, gifting Borussia Dortmund their first lead of the match. Despite five minutes of added time and a series of desperate corners from Vladimir Coufal and Mats Rots , the Dortmund defense held firm. Key clearances from Waldemar Anton and Luca Reggiani ensured the visitors completed a remarkable turnaround to claim all three points."
