      "description": "Watch 1.FC Köln vs Hoffenheim highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The Bundesliga season delivered a high-octane encounter at the RheinEnergieStadion on August 29, 2026 . 1.FC Köln hosted Hoffenheim in a match that saw tactical shifts and individual brilliance keep the 49,700 spectators on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. Hoffenheim Strike First Hoffenheim controlled much of the early proceedings, utilizing their 59% possession to dictate the tempo. Their dominance paid dividends in the 27th minute when Adam Daghim unleashed a clinical left-footed strike from outside the box, courtesy of an assist by Bambase Conte . The visitors looked comfortable for the remainder of the first half, heading into the break with a deserved lead while Köln struggled to find their rhythm in the final third. The Schwaebe Save and Dallinga’s Impact The second half ignited in the 51st minute when Said El Mala found the equalizer with a well-placed right-footed shot. The momentum swung back toward the visitors shortly after when Jahmai Simpson-Pusey conceded a penalty. However, Marvin Schwaebe produced a vital save from Max Moerstedt ’s spot-kick, a moment that proved to be a psychological turning point. Although Ozan Kabak restored Hoffenheim 's lead with a powerful header in the 67th minute, the introduction of Thijs Dallinga changed the complexion of the game. Dallinga , subbed on in the 65th minute, leveled the score at 2-2 just seven minutes later after being set up by Linton Maina . The comeback was completed in the 82nd minute when Thijs Dallinga struck again, this time with his right foot, to put the hosts ahead for the first time. Despite late pressure from Hoffenheim and a flurry of yellow cards for Ozan Kabak and Max Moerstedt for dissent, 1.FC Köln held firm to secure a dramatic three points."
